(----------------------------------------------------------------);

(Symbol 150:  Top of a cell.  This is bounded above by
a power wire, and below by ground.  Origin is the center
of the power contact of the leftmost, or pattern, inverter.
The center of the power wire is [*,0].  The center of the ground
wire is [*,-23].

Top of the cell is top of power wire: 2, except that the
clock herniates in two places, going up to 5.  The herniae
are [-15,5] to [7,5] and [39,5] to [53,5].
Contacts to diffusion can be placed on the power wire with centers
from [16,0] to [32,0].

Bottom of the cell is the bottom of the ground wire: -25.
Contacts to diffusion can be placed along the ground wire with
centers from [13,-25] to [21,-25].

The left edge is -15.  P and S both overshoot the left edge by lambda.
clock enters from left at [-15,3] to [-15,5]
	or from above at [-15,5] to [7,5]
power enters from left at [-2,-15] to [2,-15].
P enters from left at -6 to -8.
S leaves from left at -14 to -18.
ground enters from left at -21 to -25.

The right edge is at 75.  power, ground, p, and s are at the same
levels here as on the left edge.  The clock leaves from the bottom
at [68,-25] to [70,-25].

The code is divided into 5 sections:
	power and ground
	p
	d
	s
	clock
Within each section, components are specified from left to right.);
DS 150 300 1;  (units of lambda);
LNM;  B 90,4 30,0;	(power wire);
      B 90,4 30,-23;	(ground wire);

(** p--pattern from left to right on top **);
(see clock section for pass gate at input);
C 1 R 0,-1 T -8,-8;	(contact from pdiff to ppoly);
LNP;  B 4,2 T -8,-12;	(connection to inverter input);
       B 6,2 -7,-14;
C 101 T 0,0;		(p inverter);
   LND;  B 2,4 0,-19;	(connection to ground);
	C 2 T 0,-23;	(ground contact);
LNM;  B 12,4 12,-8;	(output from the p inverter);
C 2 T 20,-8;		(contact to = gate for controlled p);
LNM;  B 12,4 28,-8;	(connection between contacts);
C 11 T 31,-9;		(contact for p control of = gate);
(* controlled p--part of = gate.  This is p gated by s *);
	(gate is described in s section);
	LND;  B 4,2 24,-17;	(path in diffusion from gate to joint);
	      B 2,6 27,-19;
	      B 14,2 33,-23;
	LNP;  B 2,12 30,-15;	(connection from contact to gate);
LNM;  B 6,4 36,-8;	(connection from contact to bridge of s);
      B 2,12 40,-12;
      B 2,12 41,-12;

(** d--result goes top to bottom **);
(see clock section for pass gate at input);
LND;  B 2,18 10,-7;	(d runs vertically straight through);
      B 4,2 8,-16;	(jogs to the left);
      B 2,2 10,-16;
      B 2,10 7,-20;	(and continues);

(** s--string from right to left **);
LNM;  B 8,4 -12,-16;	(s output from cell in metal);
      B 4,4 -7,-16;	(connect bridge of p gate to s output);
LNM;  B 4,4 11,-16;	(connect bridge of p gate to s at contact);
C 11 T 14,-16;		(contact from s to poly for = control);
LNP;  B 2,2 15,-13;	(connection from contact to transistor);
C 12 T 21,-13;		(2/8 for s control of p on = gate);
LNM;  B 16,4 24,-16;	(connection between contacts);
C 2 T 34,-16;		(contact for controlled s to = gate);
C 12 T 36,-20;		(2/8 for p control of s on = gate);
LND;  B 2,4 35,-12;	(connection from s inverter output to contact);
      B 12,2 42,-11;
C 101 T 46,0;		(s inverter);
   LND;  B 12,4 T 50,-19;	(connection to ground contact);
	C 2 T 54,-23;	(ground contact);

(** clock **);
C 5 R 0,1 T -13,-7;	(clock gate on p input);
LNP;  B 2,8 -13,0;	(clock input);
      B 22,2 -4,4;	(clock goes around p inverter);
      B 2,8 6,0;	(and down to the d input);
C 5 T 10,-3;		(clock gate on d input);
LNP;  B 2,2 13,-3;	(clock leaves d gate);
      B 28,2 26,-4;	(over to s inverter);
      B 2,8 40,-1;	(up);
DF;

(ckp lost big trying to understand the complete definition of
symbol 150.  I am therefore forced to split it into two symbols.
This is the second half of the top half of a cell.  The split
is nowhere convenient, but I'll once again divide this into 5
parts.);
DS 151 300 1;		(units of lambda);
C 150 T 0,0;		(get first part.  origin in same spot);

(** p **);
LNM;  B 2,12 56,-12;	(p goes back up from bridge);
      B 2,12 57,-12;
LNM;  B 8,2 59,-7;	(connect to contact);
      B 8,2 59,-6;
C 2 T 64, -7;		(contact to diffusion);
LND;  B 6,2 69,-7;	(output in diffusion);
      B 4,2 73,-7;

(** s **);
LNP;  B 2,2 51,-14;	(connect to s inverter input);
      B 2,2 51,-15;
      B 10,2 56,-15;
C 1 M X T 64,-16;	(contact from diffusion to poly);
C 2 T 73,-16;		(contact from metal to diffusion);

(** clock **);
LNP;  B 14,2 46,4;	(clock goes around s inverter);
      B 2,8 52,0;	(and down);
      B 4,2 55,-3;	(jog over to miss side contact);
      B 2,8 56,-8;
      B 12,2 63,-11;	(over to s control);
      B 2,2 69,-11;
C 5 R 0,1 T 69,-15;	(pass gate for s input);
LNP;  B 2,8 69,-21;	(down and out);

DF;

(-----------------------------------------------------------------);
(This is a description of the pattern matcher comparator cell);

(This cell has two versions:  one for normal input, and one for
inverted input.  There is one clock line controlling the cell, and
opposite versions are expected to be controlled by opposite phases
of the two phase clock.  This description of input and output
connections applies to both versions of the cell.

Here is a schematic view of the paths through the cell:

ccccc            ccccc
5555c55d555555555c555c5555
    c  d         c   c
    cccdcccccccccc   cc
       d              c
pppppppdppppppppppppppcpp
       d              c
       d              c
sssssssdsssssssssssssscss
       d              c
     | d              c
0000-+-d00000000000000c00
     | d              c
       d              c
bbbbbbbdbbbbbbbbbbbbbbcbb
       d              c
       d              ccc
5555555d55555555555555555

The meanings of the symbols are:
	c:	clock
	5:	power
	0:	ground
	b:	bridge--this is just a path across the cell
	+:	origen of the coordinate system used to describe cell
	p:	pattern
	s:	string
	d:	downward result.

In this description, lambda is 3 microns.  The cell is 88 lambda wide,
and 49 lambda high.  The origen is the center of the ground contact for
the p inverter.  With respect to this origen, the left edge is at -16,
the right edge is at 72, the center of the lower power wire is -26,
the center of the upper power wire is 23, and the clock extends above
the upper power wire to 28.

Now we describe the connections.
Clock:	connected on left edge in poly from <-16,26> to <-16,28>
	connected on right edge in poly from <72,-23> to <72,-21>

Power1:	connected on left in metal from <-16,21> to <-16,25>
	on right in metal from <72,21> to <72,25>

p:	left in diffusion from <-16,15> to <-16,17>
	right in diffusion from <72,15> to <72,17>

s:	left in metal from <-16,5> to <-16,9>
	right in metal,diffusion, and contact from <72,5> to <72,9>

Ground:	left in metal from <-16,-2> to <-16,2>
	right in metal from <72,-2> to <72, 2>

Bridge:	left in metal from <-16,-16> to <-16,-12>
	right in metal from <72,-16> to <72,-12>

Power2:	left in metal from <-16,-24> to <-16,-28>
	right in metal from <72,-24> to <72,-28>

d:	above in diffusion from <9,25> to <11,25>
	below in diffusion from <9,-28> to <11,-28>


A pad may be placed connecting the bridge to the clock at <69,-14>);

(Symbol 160:  Negative cell.  This is the complicated one.
Origin is at the center of the ground pad of the p, or leftmost
inverter.);
(This is the negative pattern matcher cell.  It may be combined
with positive pattern matcher cells, and
with others like itself to form a complete pattern matcher.  Data
paths for p, s, and d are contained in the cell.  One phase of the 
clock comes through each cell.  Phase 2 comes through this
cell.  When that phase is high, the cell inputs pbar from the
left, sbar from the right, and dbar from above.  It then does three
computations in parallel:

	p out := NOT pbar in
	s out := NOT sbar in
	d out := NOT  [dbar in  OR NOT  p=s]
Because alternate cells have inverted signals, the bottom
half has two versions.  The top half, however, which just
computes equality and passes signal, is the same in all cells.);


DS 160 300 1;		(units of lambda);
C 151 T 0,23;		(the top half);

(** NOR gate **);
LND;  B 2,4 7,-4;	(dbar enters from the top);
      B 6,2 5,-6;	(connection to contact);
C 1 M X T 0,-7;		(contact diffusion to poly);
LND;  B 2,2 -8,-3;	(connection to pulldown);

C 2 T -8,0;		(ground contact for d half of nor);
C 3 T -8,-6;		(2/6 pulldown for d half);
LND;  B 2,6 -8,-11;	(connect to pullup);
      B 20,2 2,-13;

C 2 T 14,0;		(ground contact for not= half of nor);
LND;  B 4,4 14,-4;	(connect ground contact to pulldown);
C 14 T 14,-9;		(2/3 pulldown on not= half);
LND;  B 4,4 14,-14;	(connect pulldown to pullup);
C 13 M Y T 15,-20;	(6/2 pullup with side contact);
LND;  B 2,2 15,-25;	(connect pullup to contact);
C 2 T 18,-26;		(power contact for nor gate);

LND;  B 4,2 11,-15;	(connect d out to inverter);
LND;  B 2,8 10,-20;	(d goes out the bottom);

(** = inverter **);
C 2 T 21,0;		(ground contact for = inverter);
LND;  B 2,2 22,-3;	(connect contact to pulldown);
      B 10,2 26,-5;
      B 2,2 30,-12;
C 5 T 30,-8;			(2/2 pulldown);
C 16 M Y T 30,-19;	(8/2 pullup for = inverter);
C 2 T 30,-26;		(power contact for inverter);

LNP;  B 2,8 26,-16;	(inverter output);
      B 4,2 25,-12;	(connect to nor gate input);
      B 2,4 23,-11;
      B 6,2 21,-9;

(** The rest of the = gate **);
LND;  B 4,4 38,-3;	(connect top part to pullup);
      B 12,4 42,-4;
C 16 M Y T 46,-12;	(8/2 pullup on = gate);
LND;  B 18,2 54,-18;	(connect pullup to power);
      B 2,6 62,-21;
C 2 T 62,-26;		(power contact);

LNP;  B 4,2 35,-8;	(= gate output to inverter input);
      B 8,2 39,-9;

(** clock **);
LNP;  B 2,20 69,-12;	(clock goes straight down);
      B 8,2 72,-22;	(and over to connect to next cell);

(** Metal Bridge **);
LNM;  B 24,4 -4,-14;	(Bridge enters from the left);
      B 4,8 10,-12;	(up to miss NOR gate contact);
      B 36,4 26,-7;	(over NOR gate and inverter);
LNM;  B 4,12 42,-14;	(down to miss =gate);
      B 20,4 50,-18;	(over to the right);
	B 20,4 66,-14;	(and out);
DF;

(Symbol 161:  Negative cell, with extended = gate pullup.
Origin is at the center of the ground pad of the p, or leftmost
inverter.);
(This is the negative pattern matcher cell.  It may be combined
with positive pattern matcher cells, and
with others like itself to form a complete pattern matcher.  Data
paths for p, s, and d are contained in the cell.  One phase of the 
clock comes through each cell.  Phase 2 comes through this
cell.  When that phase is high, the cell inputs pbar from the
left, sbar from the right, and dbar from above.  It then does three
computations in parallel:

	p out := NOT pbar in
	s out := NOT sbar in
	d out := NOT  [dbar in  OR NOT  p=s]
Because alternate cells have inverted signals, the bottom
half has two versions.  The top half, however, which just
computes equality and passes signal, is the same in all cells.);


DS 161 300 1;		(units of lambda);
C 151 T 0,23;		(the top half);

(** NOR gate **);
LND;  B 2,4 7,-4;	(dbar enters from the top);
      B 6,2 5,-6;	(connection to contact);
C 1 M X T 0,-7;		(contact diffusion to poly);
LND;  B 2,2 -8,-3;	(connection to pulldown);

C 2 T -8,0;		(ground contact for d half of nor);
C 3 T -8,-6;		(2/6 pulldown for d half);
LND;  B 2,6 -8,-11;	(connect to pullup);
      B 20,2 2,-13;

C 2 T 14,0;		(ground contact for not= half of nor);
LND;  B 4,4 14,-4;	(connect ground contact to pulldown);
C 14 T 14,-9;		(2/3 pulldown on not= half);
LND;  B 4,4 14,-14;	(connect pulldown to pullup);
C 13 M Y T 15,-20;	(6/2 pullup with side contact);
LND;  B 2,2 15,-25;	(connect pullup to contact);
C 2 T 18,-26;		(power contact for nor gate);

LND;  B 4,2 11,-15;	(connect d out to inverter);
LND;  B 2,8 10,-20;	(d goes out the bottom);

(** = inverter **);
C 2 T 21,0;		(ground contact for = inverter);
LND;  B 2,2 22,-3;	(connect contact to pulldown);
      B 10,2 26,-5;
      B 2,2 30,-12;
C 5 T 30,-8;			(2/2 pulldown);
C 16 M Y T 30,-19;	(8/2 pullup for = inverter);
C 2 T 30,-26;		(power contact for inverter);

LNP;  B 2,8 26,-16;	(inverter output);
      B 4,2 25,-12;	(connect to nor gate input);
      B 2,4 23,-11;
      B 6,2 21,-9;

(** The rest of the = gate **);
LND;  B 4,4 38,-3;	(connect top part to pullup);
      B 12,4 42,-4;
C 13 M Y T 46,-11;	(6/2 pullup on = gate);
LND;  B 18,2 54,-16;	(connect pullup to power);
      B 2,8 62,-20;
LNI;	B 14,6 53,-16;	(implant for extended pullup);
LNP;	B 10,6 53,-16;	(gate for extended pullup);
LNI;	B 6,6 46,-16;	(clean up corner);
LNP;	B 6,6 46,-16;

C 2 T 62,-26;		(power contact);

LNP;  B 4,2 35,-8;	(= gate output to inverter input);
      B 8,2 39,-9;

(** clock **);
LNP;  B 2,20 69,-12;	(clock goes straight down);
      B 8,2 72,-22;	(and over to connect to next cell);

(** Metal Bridge **);
LNM;  B 24,4 -4,-14;	(Bridge enters from the left);
      B 4,8 10,-12;	(up to miss NOR gate contact);
      B 36,4 26,-7;	(over NOR gate and inverter);
LNM;  B 4,12 42,-14;	(down to miss =gate);
      B 20,4 50,-18;	(over to the right);
	B 20,4 66,-14;	(and out);
DF;


(------------------------------------------------------------);

(Symbol 170:  positive comparitor cell.  Origin is center of ground
pad of leftmost inverter.);
(This is the positive pattern matcher cell.  It may be combined
with negative pattern matcher cells, and
with others like itself to form a complete pattern matcher.  Data
paths for p, s, and d are contained in the cell.  One phase of the 
clock comes through each cell.  Phase 1 comes through this
cell.  When that phase is high, the cell inputs p from the
left, s from the right, and d from above.  It then does three
computations in parallel:

	pbar out := NOT p in
	sbar out := NOT s in
	dbar out := NOT  [d in  AND  p=s]
Because alternate cells have inverted signals, the bottom
half has two versions.  The top half, however, which just
computes equality and passes signal, is the same in all cells.);

DS 170 300 1;		(units of lambda);
C 151 T 0,23;		(top half of cell);

(** nand gate **);
C 2 T 16,0;		(ground contact for nand gate);
LND;  B 4,2 16,-3;	(connection from ground to pulldown);
C 12 T 17,-6;		(first pulldown);
C 12 T 17,-10;		(second pulldown);
C 16 M Y T 18,-19;	(8/2 pullup);
C 2 T 18,-26;		(power contact for nand gate);

(** d from top half **);
LND;  B 2,6 7,-4;	(connection from input to contact);
C 1 R 0,-1 T 6,-8;	(butting contact to gate input);
LNP;  B 4,2 10,-10;	(connection to gate input);

LND;  B 8,2 13,-13;	(nand gate output);
      B 2,10 10,-19;	(connect d to next cell down);

(** continuation of = gate from top half **);
LND;  B 6,4 34,-3;	(connection from top half);
LNP;  B 6,2 25,-6;	(connection to input of nand gate);
      B 2,6 29,-8;
C 16 M Y T 32,-12;	(8/2 pullup);
LND;  B 2,6 32,-21;	(connection to power contact);
C 2 T 32,-26;		(power contact for = gate);

(** clock **);
LNP;   B 2,20 69,-12;	(drop straight down from the top half);
	B 8,2 72,-22;	(connect to lower right);

(** Metal Bridge **);
LNM;  B 14,4 -8,-14;	(Bridge enters from the left);
      B 20,4 2,-18;	(up to miss butting contact);
LNM;  B 4,12 14,-14;	(up to cross over nand gate);
      B 16,4 20,-7;	(cross over);
      B 4,12 29,-11;	(down to cross = gate);
      B 24,4 39,-16;	(across = gate);
      B 32,4 60,-14;	(out to the right);
DF;


(Symbol 171:  positive comparitor cell.  Origin is center of ground
pad of leftmost inverter.  This has the extended = pullup.);
(This is the positive pattern matcher cell.  It may be combined
with negative pattern matcher cells, and
with others like itself to form a complete pattern matcher.  Data
paths for p, s, and d are contained in the cell.  One phase of the 
clock comes through each cell.  Phase 1 comes through this
cell.  When that phase is high, the cell inputs p from the
left, s from the right, and d from above.  It then does three
computations in parallel:

	pbar out := NOT p in
	sbar out := NOT s in
	dbar out := NOT  [d in  AND  p=s]
Because alternate cells have inverted signals, the bottom
half has two versions.  The top half, however, which just
computes equality and passes signal, is the same in all cells.);

DS 171 300 1;		(units of lambda);
C 151 T 0,23;		(top half of cell);

(** nand gate **);
C 2 T 16,0;		(ground contact for nand gate);
LND;  B 4,2 16,-3;	(connection from ground to pulldown);
C 12 T 17,-6;		(first pulldown);
C 12 T 17,-10;		(second pulldown);
C 16 M Y T 18,-19;	(8/2 pullup);
C 2 T 18,-26;		(power contact for nand gate);

(** d from top half **);
LND;  B 2,6 7,-4;	(connection from input to contact);
C 1 R 0,-1 T 6,-8;	(butting contact to gate input);
LNP;  B 4,2 10,-10;	(connection to gate input);

LND;  B 8,2 13,-13;	(nand gate output);
      B 2,10 10,-19;	(connect d to next cell down);

(** continuation of = gate from top half **);
LND;  B 6,4 34,-3;	(connection from top half);
LNP;  B 6,2 25,-6;	(connection to input of nand gate);
      B 2,6 29,-8;
C 13 M Y T 32,-11;	(6/2 pullup);
LND;	B 28,2 47,-16;	(connection to power contact);
	B 2,10 62,-20;
LNI;	B 14,6 40,-16;	(Implant for extended = gate);
LNP;	B 10,6 40,-16;	(Gate for pullup);
LNI;	B 6,6 32,-16;	(clean up corner);
LNP;	B 6,6 32,-16;
LND;	B 2,2 32,-16;
C 2 T 62,-26;		(power contact for = gate);

(** clock **);
LNP;   B 2,20 69,-12;	(drop straight down from the top half);
	B 8,2 72,-22;	(connect to lower right);

(** Metal Bridge **);
LNM;  B 14,4 -8,-14;	(Bridge enters from the left);
      B 20,4 2,-18;	(up to miss butting contact);
LNM;  B 4,12 14,-14;	(up to cross over nand gate);
      B 16,4 20,-7;	(cross over);
      B 4,12 29,-11;	(down to cross = gate);
      B 24,4 39,-16;	(across = gate);
      B 32,4 60,-14;	(out to the right);
DF;

(-----------------------------------------------------------);

(Pad hookup for one cell.  There are 9 pads for a
cell.  Starting at the upper left, and going clockwise, they are:
	ground input:
	P input
	D input
	S input
	<Symbol goes here>
	p output	<at the side>
	power input
	D output
	clock input
	S output

);
DS 210 300 1;	(units of lambda);

(** Power hookup **);
(power pad to P out pad);
LNM;	B 92,8 378,-104;	(right from power pad);
	B 8,12 420,-94;		(up to output pad);

(cell hookup);
LNM;	B 36,8 242,-104;	(horizontal out of power pad);
	B 8,88 228,-56;		(up to go around D out pad);
	B 144,8 160,-8;		(over to bus bar);
LNM;	B 88,4 28,-26;		(lowest power wire);
	B 16,4 80,23;		(hook top to bus bar);
	B 16,4 80,-26;		(hook bottom to busbar);
	B 8,50 84,-2;		(vertical bus bar);

(** Ground hookup **);
LNM;	B 24,8 -24,44;	(Ground pad to P in pad);
LNM;	B 24,8 104,44;	(P in pad to Din pad);
LNM;	B 24,8 232,44;	(D in pad to S in pad);
LNM;	B 8,12 252,34;	(S in pad to P out pad);
LNM;	B 8,64 -100,8;	(Ground pad to S out pad);
LNM;	B 4,26 -30,-11;	(S out pad to cell ground);
	B 16,4 -20,0;
LNM;	B 8,56 -32,-52;	(S out pad to clock in pad);
	B 20,8 -20,-76;
LNM;	B 16,8 100,-76;		(Clock in pad to D out pad);
	B 8,56 112,-52;

(** P input hookup **);
LND;	B 2,4 -14,38;	(out of pad to contact);
C 2 T -14,34;		(contact to metal);
LNM;	B 4,4 -18,34;	(to the left);
	B 4,20 -22,26;	(down to input);
C 2 T -22,16;		(contact to diffusion);
LND;	B 4,2 -18,16;	(into cell);
(** P output hookup **);
LND;	B 28,4 86,16;	(diffusion out of cell);
C 2 T 102,16;		(contact to metal);
LNM;	B 142,4 173,16;	(metal over to the right);
LNM;	B 4,40 242,-4;	(down to pad);
C 11 T 242,-24;		(contact from metal to poly);
LNP;	B 4,2 246,-24;	(to output pad);

(**S input hookup **);
LND;	B 2,4 242,38;	(diffusion path to contact);
C 2 T 242,34;		(contact to metal);
LNM;	B 100,4 190,34;	(metal run to the left);
	B 20,4 130,34;
	B 4,4 122,30;	(down);
	B 32,4 108,26;	(to the left again);
	B 4,16 94,18;	(down to contact);
C 2 T 94,8;		(contact from metal to gate input);
LND;	B 20,2 82,8;	(gate input in diffusion);
(** S output hookup **);
LNM;	B 74,4 -53,7;	(From cell leftward to pad);
	B 4,22 -88,-6;	(Down to contact);
C 11 T -88,-18;		(contact from metal to poly);
LNP;	B 2,4 -88,-22;	(poly into pad);

(** D input hookup **);
LND;	B 2,4 114,38;	(diffusion path to contact);
C 2 T 114,34;		(contact to metal);
LNM;	B 102,4 61,34;	(metal run to input);
C 2 T 10,34;		(contact back to diffusion);
LND;	B 2,12 10,28;	(into cell);
(** D output hookup **);
LND;	B 2,8 10,-28;	(Leave cell in diffusion);
C 2 T 10,-34;		(contact to metal);
LNM;	B 84,4 54,-34;	(metal run to end of cell);
	B 4,12 94 -26;	(up to go around output pad);
	B 76,4 130,-18;	(over to pad);
C 11 T 168,-18;		(contact from metal to poly);
LNP;	B 2,4 168,-22;	(down to gate);

(** clock hookup **);
LND;	B 2,4 -14,-70;	(diffusion path from pad to contact);
C 2 T -14,-66;		(contact to metal);
LNM;	B 8,4 -20,-66;	(path up to metal bridge);
	B 4,52 -22,-38;
	B 8,4 -16,-14;
C 11 T 69 -14;		(contact from metal to poly);

(*Upper row of 